  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe proposed method employs a trust-region derivative-free optimization strategy using the COBYLA algorithm. It is particularly suited for non-convex problems like the Erd\u0151s overlap minimization due to its ability to handle complex constraints without requiring gradient information. The approach combines global exploration through a multistart strategy with local refinement via COBYLA, aiming to escape local minima and find a better global solution.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Decision variables: h[i] \u2208 [0, 1] for i = 1, ..., n_points\n- Objective function: min t where t \u2265 max_k [dx * \u03a3 h[i](1 - h[i + k])]\n- Constraints:\n  - \u03a3 h[i] = n_points / 2\n  - 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- The problem is non-convex due to bilinear terms in the overlap integral. COBYLA is chosen for its effectiveness with such problems.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialization\n   - Use initial_h_values as the base solution\n   - Set number of perturbation starts (n_starts) based on budget\n   - Compute dx = 2.0 / n_points\n\nb. Perturbation and optimization loop\n   For each start in 1..n_starts:\n      i. Generate perturbed h by adding noise: h_perturbed = h + noise\n      ii. Clip to [0,1]: h_perturbed = np.clip(h_perturbed, 0, 1)\n      iii. Rescale to meet integral constraint: h_perturbed *= (n_points / 2) / np.sum(h_perturbed)\n      iv. Run COBYLA optimizer:\n           - Minimize overlap integral with COBYLA\n           - Use constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and \u03a3h = n_points / 2\n      v. Track best solution\n\nc. Termination\n   - Stop when time budget is exhausted or all starts are complete\n   - Return best h found\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- n_starts: 5\n- COBYLA settings:\n  - maxiter: 800\n  - rhobeg: 0.1\n  - rhoend: 1e-5\n- Perturbation noise scale: 0.1 * sqrt(1 / n_points)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Estimated runtime: 1100s\n- Robustness: Multiple starts reduce risk of local minima\n- Feasibility: Maintained through clipping and rescaling\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Ensure \u03a3h = n_points / 2 and 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- Validate C\u2085 using evaluator\n- Return best solution within time budget",
